# C1-S10 to C1-S12 — Fragment One, the Village Meeting, Elara Joins.
# Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 1830–1900.
# The first memory flash, then the first disclosure choice (Chapter 8 remembers
# it). In "fragment", Elara uses Kaelen's name for the first time in the game.

# C1-S10: a maintenance chamber everyone thinks is a shrine.
~ fragment
do touch_fragment
System: SOURCE AUTHORIZATION: ONE OF SEVEN.
do kaelen_recoils
Elara: Sit down before you fall. You went white.
Kaelen: I knew those words.
Elara: You read them. They're cut into the wall, right in front of your nose.
Kaelen: Before I read them. I knew how it ended before I got to the end.
do memory_flash
Colleague: Seven signatures for every root change? Nothing will ever get through.
Kaelen (Memory): That's the point.
do flash_ends
Elara: Kaelen? Kaelen, look at me.
Kaelen: I've been here before. That can't be right, and it is. I don't know how.
Elara: In this shrine? Nobody's been down those steps in years. Look at the dust.
Kaelen: Not in it. Under it. There's something under the floor, and it's still running.
# The scene awards it (GameManager.collect_source_key sets source_key_fragment_1
# and counts it; setting the flag here would stop it counting).
do fragment_acquired 1

# C1-S11: Oakhaven wants to know what happened.
~ meeting
do village_gathers
Mara: Well? What was it down there? Is the north field going to do that again? Is it coming for the houses, or do I move the flour?
? Kaelen (Internal): Every face in the square is turned my way. How much do I tell them?
- All of it. It spreads, and there's something old under Oakhaven that's failing. => public
- Just the people who'll have to deal with it. Not the whole square. => limited
- It's handled. That's all they need tonight. => silent

~ public
set ch1_oakhaven_warned_villagers
Kaelen: The Fracture can spread. There's something under Oakhaven, very old, and parts of it are failing. How fast, I can't tell you yet.
do villagers_panic
Mara: Can it reach the wells? Is it in them already? Do I tell the whole lane to stop drawing?
Kaelen: I don't know, and I won't guess. Not about water people drink.
Mara: Can you find out? How long do I keep the lane off the wells?
Kaelen: A day. Give me a day, and somebody who knows where the wells run.
Mara: One day, then. I'm counting it. Everybody home. Boil your water, and the washing water too.

~ limited
set ch1_oakhaven_warned_leaders
Kaelen: Bran. Mara. Can I borrow you both somewhere quieter? And whoever runs the council.
Bran: That's us, and Tobb, who's asleep. I can tell from your hands it's bad. I'll take it down for him; Tobb trusts ink over faces.

~ silent
set ch1_oakhaven_left_quietly
do trust elara -10
Kaelen: It's handled. You're safe tonight. Please, everyone, go home and sleep.
Mara: Tonight. Fine. And tomorrow? I'll be baking either way.
do elara_watches
Elara: That is not what you saw down there. You know that.
Kaelen: It's the part they can do something about. The rest would only keep them awake.
Elara: They're not children, stranger. They live on top of it.

# C1-S12: Elara packs. elara_trust_high is kept up to date by every
# "do trust elara …" in Chapter 1 (DialogueManager, TRUST_HIGH = 30).
~ joins
do elara_packs
Kaelen: You're packing. That's a lot of bandages for someone who isn't coming.
Elara: They're for me. Some of them might end up on you.
Kaelen: So that's a yes? I'd like it out loud. I can't read people while they're folding things.
Elara: You can't read people, full stop. Pass me that cloak, and mind the patches.
[if elara_trust_high] => joins_high
=> joins_low

~ joins_low
Elara: Let us be clear. I am not following you.
Kaelen: You've had that one ready since the meeting, haven't you?
Elara: I am following whatever keeps making my arm worse. You happen to be standing next to it.
=> joined

~ joins_high
Elara: Somebody has to stop you rewriting a horse because it looks tired.
Kaelen: I'd only look at it. Looking's harmless.
Elara: You look at things, and then they're different. I've watched you do it since the crater.
Kaelen: ...I'd probably leave the horse alone.
Elara: That's why I'm packing.
Elara: Come on, Kaelen. You're carrying the herbs. Don't sit on them.
=> joined

~ joined
set ch1_elara_joined
do elara_joins_party
